# EXP-29: Rule-based Classification vs Decision Tree Classification in WEKA

======================================================================
  EXPERIMENT 29: RULE-BASED (JRIP) VS DECISION TREE (J48) IN WEKA
======================================================================

1. OBJECTIVE:
   To compare Rule-based Classification (JRip / RIPPER algorithm) with Decision 
   Tree Classification (J48) in WEKA and analyze rule interpretability.

2. WEKA EXECUTION STEPS:
   a. Classify tab -> Select Classifier:
      - JRip: weka.classifiers.rules.JRip
      - J48: weka.classifiers.trees.J48
   b. Run 10-fold cross-validation.

3. WEKA OUTPUT LOG & COMPARISON:
======================================================================
=== JRip Rules Output ===
(Petal-Width <= 0.8) => Species=setosa (50.0/0.0)
(Petal-Width <= 1.7) and (Petal-Length <= 4.9) => Species=versicolor (48.0/1.0)
 => Species=virginica (52.0/3.0)

Number of Rules : 3

